        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "07411dc6-6e6b-50d3-ba14-e6b34724002a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Television series: Mixels, Legends of Chima, Nicky, Ricky, Dicky & Dawn, The Loud House\n- Companies: The Lego Group, Cartoon Network Studios, Atomic Cartoons, Digital eMation, Big Star Entertainment, Saerom Animation, Nickelodeon, Cartoon Network\n- People: Brian Stepanek\n- Products: Toon Boom Harmony, LEGO Legends of Chima sets\n- Roles: Tom Harper, Lynn Loud Sr., Magnifo\n\nFacts:\n- Legends of Chima began with two episodes airing on January 16, 2013, and its first season ended on December 5, 2013.\n- Legends of Chima is a CGI animated television series based on the LEGO Legends of Chima line of LEGO sets.\n- Mixels was a 2014 comedy animated television series that aired on Cartoon Network and was co-produced by The Lego Group and Cartoon Network Studios.\n- Mixels used Toon Boom Harmony software and was animated at Atomic Cartoons before later being animated traditionally at Digital eMation, Big Star Entertainment, and Saerom Animation.\n- Previous Lego television series such as Legends of Chima used CGI animation.\n- Brian Stepanek played Tom Harper on Nickelodeon's Nicky, Ricky, Dicky & Dawn, voiced Lynn Loud Sr. on Nickelodeon's The Loud House, and voiced Magnifo on Cartoon Network's shortform series Mixels.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f13c1e60-b813-5b3b-9076-57e32b32a690",
        "text": "Page: Mixels. Sentence: Mixels was a 2014 comedy animated television series that aired on Cartoon Network, co-produced by The Lego Group and Cartoon Network Studios.\nPage: Mixels. Sentence: Although previous Lego series, such as \"\" and \"Legends of Chima\" use CGI animation, \"Mixels\" made use of Toon Boom Harmony software, which is animated at Atomic Cartoons, Inc., before later being animated traditionally at Digital eMation, Inc., Big Star Entertainment, Inc., and Saerom Animation, Inc..\nPage: Legends of Chima. Sentence: Legends of Chima is a CGI animated television series based on the LEGO Legends of Chima series of LEGO sets.\nPage: Legends of Chima. Sentence: It began with 2 episodes airing on January 16, 2013, with the Season 1 finale on December 5, 2013.\nPage: Brian Stepanek. Sentence: He is now known for playing Tom Harper on the Nickelodeon series \"Nicky, Ricky, Dicky & Dawn\"; the voice of Lynn Loud Sr. on the Nickelodeon animated series \"The Loud House\"; and as the voice of Magnifo on the shortform Cartoon Network series \"Mixels\".",
